      "title": "M2.1 · Score ⇄ Sequence",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "M2.1: Score to Sequence and back.\n\nA two-part score (flute, cello) with a tempo change (90, then 120 BPM in bar 3), dynamics, staccato/tenuto/accent, \"pizz.\"/\"arco\", a tie across the barline and a quarter-flat B in the flute.\n\nPress Run. Look at:\n1. Original score (top middle).\n2. Sequence Viewer: the same notes at their times in ms, one staff per part. The run after the tempo change is visibly faster. Dynamics and pizz./arco show on the notes, and the quarter-flat B carries -50 cents.\n3. Back to a score: Sequence to Score quantizes the Sequence again at one tempo (90 BPM, sixteenth grid). The first bars come back as written (pitches, ties, staccato/tenuto/accent, dynamics, pizz./arco). The fast run at 120 BPM gets approximate, overlapping rhythms, because a Sequence has no tempo map yet (M2.2); the overlaps make music21 split the flute into two voices, hence the extra rests above the staff. Gaps between notes are not written as rests yet.\n\nTry: Score to Sequence bpm (0 = use the score's tempo marks), Sequence to Score quantization (\"none\" keeps exact times) and bpm. Swap the path for any MusicXML/MIDI file."
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    }
